{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/09 17:40 SAST
Version: 0.7
Description:
  The tag page: the cloud, and the courses of whichever tag is chosen.

  Landing here shows the vocabulary and nothing else. A reader has not asked for any courses yet,
  and the whole catalogue is not an answer to a question nobody asked. Choosing a tag, or
  searching, puts the courses below the cloud - so the cloud stays on screen and a second tag is
  one click away rather than a trip back.

  This is the only tag cloud on the platform. The categories page used to draw one as well, which
  meant two clouds disagreeing about how many tags were worth showing.

  A tag holding nothing is still listed, greyed rather than hidden: this page is telling a reader
  what the vocabulary is, and a term nobody has used yet is part of that.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code.
Changelog:
  2026/09/09 17:40 SAST
  - Became the tag page proper: the cloud stays, and a chosen tag lists its courses below it, searched and paginated.
#}
{% extends layout %}
{% block page_body %}
	{% set ph_back_href = '/courses' %}
	{% set ph_back_label = 'Browse by category' %}
	{% set ph_kicker = 'Browse' %}
	{% set ph_title = selected_tag ? 'Courses tagged ' ~ selected_tag.name : 'Browse by tag' %}
	{% set ph_lead = selected_tag ? 'Choose another tag to move across the catalogue.' : 'Every label in the catalogue. The larger a tag, the more courses carry it. Choose one to see its courses.' %}
	{% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}
	<section class="container-fluid cl-container-wide py-4">
		{% if tag_index %}
{#
			The importmap goes before any module script on the page. Themes put the platform's own
			scripts at the end of the body, so emitting it here keeps it first without asking five
			themes to carry a tag for one page.
#}
			{{ importmap() }}
			<div class="cl-facet section cl-tag-cloud-shell" {{ stimulus_controller('tag-cloud') }}>
				<div class="cl-facet-head">
					<span class="cl-facet-label">Tags</span>
					{% if selected_tag %}
						<a class="btn btn-soft btn-sm" href="/courses/tags">Clear tag</a>
					{% endif %}
				</div>
{#
				Two renderings of the same thing. The list is what the server sends and what a reader
				without JavaScript keeps; the canvas is what the Stimulus controller fills, and it
				hides the list only once it has something to show in its place.
#}
				<div {{ stimulus_target('tag-cloud', 'source') }}>
					{% include '@platform/partials/tag-cloud.html.twig' with {cloud_tags: tag_index} %}
				</div>
				<div class="cl-tag-cloud-canvas" {{ stimulus_target('tag-cloud', 'canvas') }} aria-hidden="true"></div>
			</div>
		{% else %}
			<div class="empty section">
				<h3>
					No tags have been created yet
				</h3>
			</div>
		{% endif %}
		{% include '@platform/partials/dataset-search.html.twig' with {ds_name: 'catalogue', ds_label: 'Search courses', ds_value: catalogue_search, ds_action: catalogue_pagination.base} %}
		<div id="catalogue-region" data-server-search-target>
			<div id="catalogue-results">
				{% if showing_courses %}
					{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: catalogue_pagination} %}
					{% if courses %}
						<div class="cl-course-cards section">
							{% for course in courses %}
								{% include '@platform/partials/course-card.html.twig' with {course: course} %}
							{% endfor %}
						</div>
					{% else %}
						<div class="empty section">
							<h3>
								Nothing carries that tag yet
							</h3>
						</div>
					{% endif %}
					{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: catalogue_pagination} %}
				{% endif %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
{% endblock %}
